    "result_text": "All tests pass. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What I implemented\n\nA structured address form for `POST /api/owners`, backward-compatible with the flat `address` input.\n\n**Contract (`openapi.yml` \u2014 `OwnerFields` schema)**\n- Added optional `addressLine1` and `addressLine2` properties.\n- Rewrote `address` to document it as the composed, normalized output value.\n- Removed `address` from the `required` list (an owner is now valid with *either* a non-blank `addressLine1` *or* the flat `address`, plus `city`), keeping earlier minimal owners accepted.\n\n**Validation & composition (`RequireOwnerFields.java`)** \u2014 the first step of the create pipeline:\n- Normalizes whichever address fields are supplied (via the existing `AddressNormalizer`).\n- Prefers the structured form when `addressLine1` is non-blank; otherwise uses the flat `address`.\n- Composes the canonical `address` = normalized `addressLine1`, with a single space + normalized `addressLine2` appended only when `addressLine2` is present.\n- Sets that composed value on the request early, so every later step reading `getAddress()` (which flows into the household hash, postcode validation, locality, and the stored entity) sees the structured-when-present value and falls back to flat otherwise.\n- The existing blank-address check now naturally rejects a request that supplies an address in neither form.\n\n**Persistence**\n- Added `addressLine1` / `addressLine2` fields + accessors to the `Owner` entity (MapStruct auto-maps them in and out).\n- Added `address_line1` / `address_line2` columns (at table end) to all four schema dialects (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) and appended the two matching NULLs to the hsqldb positional seed rows.\n\n## Tests\n- `AcceptanceTest.coreNormalizesAndComposesStructuredAddress` \u2014 passes (`addressLine1` \u2192 `\"10 KING STREET\"`, composed `address` \u2192 `\"10 KING STREET\"`).\n- `AcceptanceTest.functionalityStillAcceptsFlatAddress` \u2014 passes (flat form still accepted).\n- Full suite: **BUILD SUCCESS**, 2/2 green.\n\nOne note: mysql's `data.sql` positional seed inserts were already inconsistent with the mysql schema before this change (fewer values than columns) and are not exercised by the test profile (hsqldb), so I left them untouched rather than mask a pre-existing discrepancy.",
